-- 660_holiday_couple_corridor_seed_repair.sql — fall + Halloween COUPLE seeds (dual_scenarios) that stage the couple
-- on a route get a spot beside it, same place and theme (2026-10-02, NIGHTLY_COMPOSITION_AUDIT_PLAN.md).
--
-- Composition audit of 2,346 delivered nightlies: couples on route-word holiday seeds were route-staged 51-57% vs
-- 11-16% without; under today's couple composer (since 09-18) 33% vs 16%. Render test on Kevin's account before any
-- row changed: 10 route seeds, each replayed through the real nightly-dreams (force_slot_input on a fresh couple
-- template of the same sub-theme) 4x with the original seed and 4x reworded: route-staged 11/40 -> 3/40, swap health
-- equal (2 fallbacks each arm). Wins: decorated neighborhood 4/4 -> 0/4, headless-hollow bridge 3/4 -> 0/4, werewolf
-- forest 3/4 -> 1/4. No gain on a dock seed (0/2 -> 1/2) and small losses where the rewrite still named a maze or a
-- switchback, so those are NOT applied: 48 dock/pier seeds, the corn-maze and switchback sub-themes, 9 others.
--
-- 352 rows (scripts/fix-holiday-corridor-seeds.js --table dual), every rewrite read by hand, 21 edited by hand; the
-- dual-swap proximity lint (scripts/lib/posePoolLint.js, the scan's own patterns) run on every rewrite: 0 violations.
-- Every statement is guarded (still the old text), so a re-run changes nothing.
-- ROLLBACK: swap each statement's SET and WHERE text (the tool's --rollback writes it).

